# Qwen3.8-27B on a 24 GB card — the tuned profile
#
# Restore with:
#     cp docs/profiles/qwen38-27b.env .env
#     $EDITOR .env                          # MODELS_DIR is machine-specific
#     ./scripts/serve.sh up
#
# These are not defaults. Every value below was measured; EXPERIMENTS.md records
# what each one was compared against, including the settings that came out worse.
# Verified in production on an RTX 3090: 21,074 of 24,576 MiB, 63.2 t/s decode
# under real agent load.

# --- Where the .gguf files live on the host ---
# Machine-specific. Mounted read-only at /models inside the container.
MODELS_DIR=/home/nromero/models

# --- Model ---
MODEL_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
MODEL_ALIAS=qwen38-27b
CONTAINER_NAME=qwen
PORT=8080

# --- Memory ---
# 65536 rather than the 131072 this card could hold: peak context under real
# agent load was 22,564 tokens, and llama.cpp allocates the whole KV cache at
# load time. The trigger to raise it is `truncated = 1` in the logs, not free
# VRAM. EXPERIMENTS.md section 7.
CTX=65536
NGL=all
# q8_0 costs half of f16 at negligible loss. This model is hybrid — only 17 of
# its 65 blocks carry KV — so this works out to 36.1 KiB/token, or 2,312 MiB at
# the context above. EXPERIMENTS.md section 6.
KV_TYPE=q8_0

# --- Sampling: from the Qwen3 model card ---
# CAREFUL: model-specific. Ornith 1.0 35B wants --temp 1.0 --top-k 0. The
# general.sampling.* keys inside the .gguf are unreliable and disagree with the
# card — trust the card. docs/models.md section 2.
TEMP=0.6
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=20
MIN_P=0.0
REASONING_FORMAT=deepseek

# --- Throughput ---
# Raised from the 8192 default after the log showed evictions ("making room for
# prompt cache entry"), which force a full reprocess: 35 s to first token on a
# 48k context. Measured effect: 71% of prompt tokens served from cache.
# This is HOST RAM, not VRAM. 27 GB on the reference box, so 10 GB is near the
# ceiling — check `free -g` before raising it. On macOS it comes out of the same
# unified pool as the weights; start much lower there.
CACHE_RAM=10240

# llama.cpp's own defaults. The previous 512/256 was throttling prefill.
BATCH=2048
UBATCH=512

# This model ships MTP heads (blk.64.nextn.*), which ngram-simple left loaded
# but unused. draft-mtp drafts with them: lossless, no second model, no extra
# weights. Measured +31% decode. NOT PORTABLE — most models have no MTP heads;
# run scripts/gguf-info.py before reusing this line elsewhere.
SPEC_TYPE=draft-mtp
# Mean accepted length is 3.4-4.7, so a budget of 8 already goes unspent;
# raising it further measures nothing. Loosening P_MIN to 0.5 measured WORSE
# (52.0 vs 53.5 t/s): acceptance halved and the wasted compute ate the gain.
SPEC_N_MAX=8
SPEC_P_MIN=0.7

# --- Exposure ---
# Loopback only. The server has NO authentication; this is the entire access
# control story. tailscale serve proxies to 127.0.0.1:8080, so this must stay
# as it is for TLS to work. README section 7.
BIND=127.0.0.1
